course: dictionary
lesson: 698
title: A grand banquet
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A banquet is a large, formal meal for many people. People hold one to celebrate something special, and there are often speeches. It is a noun, so you can have one banquet or many banquets.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «A very old banqueting-hall (a big dining hall for feasts).» The word banqueting-hall is built from banquet, so it must be a room where big meals are held. The brackets help too: a feast is a great meal.
explain: Banquets are not only in old stories. Schools and clubs hold them today, often to celebrate awards. When you meet a word like this, ask: what would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some stories use a banquet as a picture. In a parable, Jesus told about a great banquet to show that God invites everyone. Knowing the word helps you see what the story is really saying.
fact: A banquet is a large, formal meal for many people.
fact: A banquet is usually held to celebrate something, and it often has speeches.
fact: Kings in history held banquets in great halls, with roast meat.
fact: Schools and clubs today hold banquets for awards.
fact: Phrases to know: hold a banquet, a wedding banquet, banquet hall.
exercise: «A very old banqueting-hall (a big dining hall for feasts).» What is a banqueting-hall for? | Swimming races | Stables for horses | Sleeping in | *Big feasts
exercise: Why might a school hold a banquet? | *To celebrate awards | To fix a broken door | To sell old books | Playing football all day
exercise: Find and copy the word that means a grand meal for many people. | very | *feast | stables | door
test: Badger will order the Banquet; Toad must write the invitations. Who writes the invitations? | The Banquet | *Toad | Nobody | Badger
test: What does a banquet usually celebrate? | Going to bed early | Bad weather | A lost dog | *Something special
exam: In Jesus's parable of the great banquet, what does the banquet show? | Banquets are only for kings | *That God invites everyone | Food is always cold | Guests should make excuses
